    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0272" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/7137: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-03T20:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 3,
                                1919, 8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 4, 3:35
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>4503. Council of the Heads of Delegations met Thursday morning, October 2d.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>6. With regard to the method of communicating the decision of the Council
                    regarding the blockade of Soviet Russia to neutral governments, the Council
                    decided that Mr. Clemenceau as President
                    of the Peace Conference should address a note to the diplomatic representatives
                    of the neutral powers at Paris.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Polk</hi></signed>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
